"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[1219],{1219:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/and-then-there-were-none.png\\"\\n          title=\\"And Then There Were None\\"\\n          author=\\"Agatha Christie\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Golden Bough\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2013-05-27\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9788982737022\\"\\n          rating=4.5\\n          tags=\\"mystery\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nA work called one of the world\'s top three mystery novels, I think it\'s a timeless masterpiece.  \\n<br>\\nThe story begins when eight men and women who seem to have no connection to each other are invited to a luxurious mansion on \'Indian Island\', a remote island off the Devon coast, by a mysterious figure named \'U. N. Owen\'.  \\nUpon arriving at the island, they learn that the host who invited them is absent, and only a servant couple who had arrived first welcomes them.  \\nThus, eight guests and two servants, a total of ten people, are isolated on the island.  \\n<br>\\nAfter dinner, a mysterious voice suddenly flows from a gramophone, exposing one by one the \'murder\' charges of all ten people on the island, who had cleverly evaded legal judgment in the past, along with their names.  \\n<br>\\nAs they fall into shock and confusion, people start dying one by one, exactly like the lyrics of the nursery rhyme ```Ten Little Indians```.  \\n<br>\\nIt\'s like a dark fable asking the meaning of justice.  "}')}}]);